#
# CardDemo migration | services/common-lib/src/main/resources/META-INF/spring/
#                      org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports
#
# Purpose: the one auto-configuration class the shared kernel contributes, named so that every service
#       putting this module on its path receives the correlation filter, the common-tag meter filter,
#       the money codec module and the single error advice without declaring any of them.
#
# WHY : Refactoring Rationale: this file is the reason the shared kernel now owns a resources
#       directory, and it is the whole of that directory's contents. Before it existed, four
#       cross-cutting components lived in package roots that no service scans -- a service scans its
#       own bounded context's root -- so each was compiled and tested and then instantiated by
#       nothing. The symptom was silent: log lines with no correlation identity, meters with no
#       service dimension, and failed requests rendered by the framework's own default shape.
#
# WHY : Alternatives Considered: an explicit import in each service's configuration package. Rejected
#       because a registration a service has to remember is one a service can omit, and omitting it
#       produces a service that starts and serves requests while emitting none of the above. That is
#       the same argument the error package's charter makes for reaching its advice by propagation
#       rather than by an invocation written at each of fourteen call sites.
#
# WHY : Trade-offs: this file makes the module's jar carry a resource, which the module charters
#       describe as something a library-not-a-deployable does not have. The departure is accepted
#       because there is no other mechanism by which a library contributes a bean to a consumer that
#       has not been told to look for it. It does NOT make the module configurable: this file names one
#       class and holds nothing else, no property is read from a resource, and no message text is
#       externalised -- the sibling carddemo-common-defaults.yml carries only values a service imports
#       deliberately and can override.
#
com.carddemo.common.CardDemoCommonAutoConfiguration
